 report a call to a registered user fn that provably throws \x2014;\n  either a WRONG ARITY (the registered fn has one fixed arity, so a different\n  arg count always throws) or an argument whose concrete type the body\n  rejects. For the latter, re-check the body with ONLY that parameter bound to\n  its arg type (others :any); a diagnostic the all-:any body did not already\n  have means the argument alone is provably wrong. Monotonic \x2014; binding a\n  concrete type can only ADD error-domain hits \x2014; so no false positive.\n  Cycle-guarded (env's checking-set) so mutually recursive fns terminate." (keyword #f "line") 929 (keyword #f "column") 1))))
